{"duration_api_ms":129803,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9c5ba33d-4d4c-4e1a-b42d-fb20ccd8f15d","total_cost_usd":0.190336,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15258,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":12930,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":8283},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15258,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12930,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15258,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15258},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12930,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15258,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.190336,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":8283,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Every non-dominated point comes from one family: D≈3.38 m, bluntness 1.2, cone 70 deg, with only flight-path angle varied. Along it flux rises from 228k to 275k W/m2 and bondline temperature falls from 418 K to 391 K as entry steepens. max_g (about 12 at gamma≈-3.57) and the mass-fraction limit (D<~3.3855 m) are the binding constraints. Bluntness and cone are pinned at the edge of the aero surrogate's hull. Bluntness 1.21 or more fails at cone 70, and cone 69 fails at bluntness 1.2. Smaller-D, lower-bluntness, lower-cone designs are clearly dominated. The remaining gains are small: a slightly larger D and a denser gamma sweep.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-733cdcb996ae (D 3.385, gamma -3.5) gives 272900 W/m2 / 391.77 K, against 273480 / 391.85 for C-41b2ddb7397c (D 3.38, same gamma). Larger D dominates slightly, and its mass margin is only 0.000145.\",\"Mass margin is independent of gamma (0.003097 across the D 3.38 sweep) and falls about 0.59 per metre of D. That puts the limit near D≈3.3855, so I keep D=3.385.\",\"max_g at D 3.38 is 11.881 at -3.5, 11.963 at -3.55 and 11.989 at -3.565. C-2a109f1c4205 (D 3.36, -3.58) gives 12.006 and is infeasible, so the g limit sits near gamma≈-3.57. D changes g only weakly (about +0.4 per m).\",\"C-3d41ce848a30, C-98457c6f78bd, C-ae614eb129f2 and others show that bluntness above 1.2 or cone below 70 at bluntness 1.2 hits surrogate extrapolation and returns no metrics.\",\"Off-family designs such as C-22c8ef75dedb (322k, 395.7 K, infeasible), C-960c10206981 and C-ee99f55de428 are worse in flux or temperature than the D 3.38 family.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak flux falls with larger nose radius and lower ballistic coefficient, so the largest D that meets the mass limit is best. Peak g is set almost entirely by gamma, so it caps steepness at about -3.57. Bondline temperature falls with steeper entry, so the best designs sit at the g limit. I have no data suggesting another geometry beats this family, so I refine it: D=3.385 for a small uniform gain, and a denser gamma sweep including points just inside the g limit. Interpolated values come from the D 3.38 sweep with a D correction of about -0.2% flux and -0.08 K.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The main risk is the g margin near gamma -3.56 to -3.568, where I estimate g at 11.99-11.996 against a limit of 12. Whether bluntness 1.205 lies inside the surrogate hull is unknown, and that probe may return no geometry. Gains per point are tiny (about 0.2% flux, 0.1 K). The reduced-order model's own noise or discreteness could exceed them. No other region has been shown to be promising.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow end of the front at the larger D; should slightly dominate C-d67ebd910866.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227230,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front at the low-flux extreme with a slightly better D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.7 at D 3.385.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229220,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.28,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a front point in the shallow-entry region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolated gamma point on the D 3.385 front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":233310,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.07,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front for hypervolume coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolated gamma point on the D 3.385 front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237630,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.03,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front for hypervolume coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolated gamma point on the D 3.385 front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":24